<title>USA: Exxon says French court rules against Lubrizol.</title>
<headline>Exxon says French court rules against Lubrizol.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Exxon Chemical Co said on Friday that a French appeals court in Paris has dismissed a suit brought by Lubrizol Corp in a case where Lubrizol alleged that Exxon's motor oils and motor oil additives infringed Lubrizol's Meinhardt patent.</p>
<p>The Exxon Corp unit said it expected to be awarded some defence costs in the ruling against Wycliffe, Ohio, based Lubrizol.</p>
<p>Exxon said Lubrizol had now lost three patent related suits on Europe, one of which in Britain had resulted in the payment of $11 million costs to Exxon.</p>
<p>&quot;We hope that Lubrizol reconsiders the wisdom of its frequent resort to the courts. We at Exxon prefer to focus our competition on the marketplace rather than the courts,&quot; said Ray Nesbitt, president of Exxon Chemical Co.</p>
<p>((-- David Chance New York Newsroom 212 859 1902))</p>
</text>
